\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Signed zeros on the momentum grid}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{The centered symbol
#{\ui\sum_j(\varepsilon_j^{S}\otimes\bbI_F)\sin p_j} vanishes
where every #{p_j} is #{0} or #{\pi}, and near each such corner
each coordinate equal to #{\pi} reverses its generator (\ref{fdip-009R}). The Wilson
term of \ref{fdip-009V} lifts every zero block except the one at
#{p=0}. On a finite grid the symbol is a function on finitely many
momenta. Can its zeros carry signs, and must those signs
balance?}

\p{The signs are defined for any function from the grid to
#{k^n} over an ordered field, and then applied to symbols built
from the generators.}
